---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro'
import { REPO } from '../lib/nav'
---

<Site
  title="Using the name and artwork"
  description="What you can do with Nurblings, its avatars, its name and the Nurbi artwork, and when to ask first."
  class="usage"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Using the name and artwork</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The code and every avatar it makes are yours to use. The names Nurblings and Nurbi, and the Nurbi artwork,
        are reserved, so that copies are never mistaken for this project.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="rules">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Free to use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The library and every avatar it generates, in any project, commercial or not.</li>
          <li>Generated avatars are public domain under CC0: no attribution needed.</li>
          <li>Saying your project uses, or is built with, Nurblings.</li>
          <li>Forking the code under MIT, with a name of your own.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Ask first</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Publishing a fork, package or service under the Nurblings or Nurbi name.</li>
          <li>Using Nurbi as a mascot, logo or endorsement.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="more">
      Read the full terms in <a href={`${REPO}/blob/develop/TRADEMARKS.md`}>TRADEMARKS.md</a>. For anything
      else, <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>open an issue on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Site>

<style is:global>
  .usage .rules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .usage .rules h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .usage .rules ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .usage .more {
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-block: 28px 40px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .usage .rules {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
